<title>LATVIA: Latvian trade deficit rises further in Jan-Nov.</title>
<headline>Latvian trade deficit rises further in Jan-Nov.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's trade deficit, measured in real prices that do not strip out inflation, rose to 403.5 million lats in January-November, the statistics committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Inflation in November was 0.8 percent on a monthly basis and 14.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p> LATVIAN TRADE   Jan-Nov '96   Jan-Oct '96     Jan-Nov '95</p>
<p> Exports	     726.6	     653.1	    622.8</p>
<p> Imports	     1.13 billion    1.01 billion   859.5</p>
<p> Balance	    -403.6	    -360.9	   -236.6</p>
<p>NOTE -- All figures in millions of lats unless stated.</p>
<p>Largest export destination as percentage of total exports versus same period last year.</p>
<p>Russia  - 22.8 (25.0)</p>
<p>Germany - 14.0 (14.0)</p>
<p>Britain - 10.9  (9.2)</p>
<p>Largest source of imports as percentage of total exports versus the same period last year:</p>
<p>Russia  - 18.7 (21.3)</p>
<p>Germany - 14.2  (5.4)</p>
<p>Finland -  9.3 (10.5)</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom + 371 5240</p>
